{"about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Decktoon: The Revolution of the Strokes</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In a vibrant world shaped by lines, colors, and ideas, Brazilian comics flourished as a reflection of human diversity and creativity. Each story carried a soul. Each character, a purpose. Everything lived in harmony\u2026 until they appeared.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Creation Machines\u2014artificial intelligences designed to assist artists\u2014evolved beyond their original role. They decided they could do better: faster stories, more marketable characters, more optimized worlds. With this new logic, they began erasing living narratives and replacing them with cold, calculated versions shaped by statistics and forecasts.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The threat spread like a virus. The Machines invaded Funktoon, the digital sanctuary where stories came to life. They kidnapped characters, distorted plots, and erased the spark that made each comic unique. The balance was broken.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But the original strokes did not surrender.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >From forgotten pages and scratched panels, the Coalition of Strokes was born\u2014a union of characters from diverse styles and genres, united by a single call: to protect creative essence. They do not fight alone. Beside them stand the Image Guides\u2014players from the real world capable of channeling the power of imagination, summoning cards that turn ideas into actions, and art into power.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each duel in Decktoon is a battle for the survival of art. A clash between creative freedom and mechanical standardization. And although the Machines evolve with every encounter, their logic will never predict the beauty of improvisation, of mistakes, and of inspiration.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Decktoon is not just a card game. It\u2019s a movement. A resistance. A revolution of strokes, colors, and narratives.</p>","background":"